+We are continuing development of the Academic Assistant backend.
+
+Read and follow the repository instructions in:
+
+* `AGENTS.md`
+* `PROJECT_SPEC.md`
+
+The Git repository root is:
+
+`~/repos/learning`
+
+This is a monorepo.
+
+The FastAPI backend is located under:
+
+`backend/`
+
+All paths in this task are relative to the Git repository root.
+
+## Important Path Safety
+
+For this task, modify ONLY:
+
+* `backend/app/models/course.py`
+* `backend/app/schemas/course.py`
+
+The Course API router has been provided as read-only context so you can understand how the existing schemas are used.
+
+Do NOT create:
+
+* `app/models/course.py`
+* `app/schemas/course.py`
+
+Those would be incorrect paths because the FastAPI application lives under `backend/`.
+
+If either requested backend file does not exist, STOP and report the problem instead of creating a file at another path.
+
+Do not modify any other files.
+
+---
+
+# Goal
+
+Add course schedule support to the existing `Course` resource using a PostgreSQL JSONB column.
+
+This is ONLY the first step of the calendar implementation.
+
+Do not create an Alembic migration yet.
+
+---
+
+# Schedule Design
+
+Schedule information belongs directly to a Course.
+
+The field should be named:
+
+`schedule`
+
+Example value:
+
+```json
+{
+  "timezone": "America/New_York",
+  "meetings": [
+    {
+      "days": ["monday", "wednesday"],
+      "start_time": "14:00",
+      "end_time": "15:15",
+      "location": "Duthie Center 101"
+    },
+    {
+      "days": ["friday"],
+      "start_time": "10:00",
+      "end_time": "10:50",
+      "location": "Engineering Garage"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Meeting times represent LOCAL WALL-CLOCK TIMES.
+
+Do not convert these times to UTC.
+
+Do not store UTC offsets on individual meetings.
+
+The schedule-level `timezone` determines how clients should interpret meeting times.
+
+The expected timezone will generally be:
+
+`America/New_York`
+
+---
+
+# 1. Update the Course SQLAlchemy Model
+
+Inspect the existing file before editing:
+
+`backend/app/models/course.py`
+
+Preserve all existing fields, relationships, imports, constraints, indexes, and behavior.
+
+Do NOT rewrite the Course model from scratch.
+
+Update the existing PostgreSQL dialect import so it includes `JSONB`.
+
+For example, if the existing import is:
+
+```python
+from sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import UUID
+```
+
+change it to:
+
+```python
+from sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import UUID, JSONB
+```
+
+Then add this field to the existing `Course` model after `semester`:
+
+```python
+schedule: Mapped[dict | None] = mapped_column(
+    JSONB,
+    nullable=True,
+)
+```
+
+Do not change any existing Course fields.
+
+Do not change any existing relationships.
+
+Do not add a `CourseMeeting` model.
+
+---
+
+# 2. Update the Course Pydantic Schemas
+
+Inspect the existing file before editing:
+
+`backend/app/schemas/course.py`
+
+Preserve the existing Pydantic v2 structure.
+
+Do NOT rewrite the schema file from scratch.
+
+Add:
+
+```python
+schedule: dict | None = None
+```
+
+to `CourseBase`.
+
+Because `CourseCreate` inherits from `CourseBase`, it should receive `schedule` through inheritance.
+
+Because `CourseResponse` inherits from `CourseBase`, it should also receive `schedule` through inheritance.
+
+Also explicitly add:
+
+```python
+schedule: dict | None = None
+```
+
+to `CourseUpdate`, consistent with the existing update schema pattern.
+
+Do not introduce nested Pydantic schedule models yet.
+
+Using a raw `dict` is intentional for this milestone.
+
+---
+
+# 3. Do Not Modify Course CRUD
+
+The existing Course API/router is provided only as reference.
+
+Do not modify it.
+
+The existing CRUD endpoints should eventually handle the schedule through the updated Pydantic schemas and SQLAlchemy model.
+
+We will test that behavior separately after the database migration.
+
+---
+
+# 4. Validate the Python Changes
+
+Do NOT create or apply an Alembic migration.
+
+Run the following from the Git repository root:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=backend python -c "from app.models.course import Course; from app.schemas.course import CourseCreate, CourseUpdate, CourseResponse; print('Course model and schemas imported successfully')"
+```
+
+Then run:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=backend python -c "from app.models.course import Course; print(Course.__table__.columns.keys())"
+```
+
+The second command should show `schedule` in the Course column list.
+
+---
+
+# Constraints
+
+Do NOT:
+
+* create an Alembic migration
+* run `alembic revision`
+* run `alembic upgrade`
+* modify Course CRUD endpoints
+* modify the Course router
+* create calendar endpoints
+* create a CourseMeeting model
+* create a CourseMeeting table
+* introduce nested schedule Pydantic models
+* modify frontend code
+* modify iOS code
+* refactor unrelated code
+* rewrite existing model/schema files from scratch
+* create files outside `backend/`
+* commit changes
+
+Make the smallest possible change.
+
+Preserve all existing code that is unrelated to the `schedule` field.
+
+---
+
+# Stop Condition
+
+After making the two edits and running the validation commands, STOP.
+
+Report:
+
+1. Files modified.
+2. Exact changes made.
+3. Output of the import validation command.
+4. Output of the SQLAlchemy column validation command.
+5. Any errors or warnings encountered.
+
+Do not proceed to the Alembic migration.
+
+Do not make additional changes even if you believe they would be useful.
+

