# 2026-08-18 21:17:23.566478
+Create only the frontend authentication API helper.
+
+Use the existing FastAPI authentication contract you just inspected.
+
+Requirements:
+
+* JavaScript only.
+* Do not modify any backend files.
+* Do not build the login page yet.
+* Do not create Next.js API routes.
+* Do not implement JWT storage yet.
+* Do not redirect anywhere yet.
+* Keep the implementation simple.
+
+Create:
+
+`frontend/src/lib/auth-api.js`
+
+Implement two functions:
+
+1. `login(email, password)`
+
+This function must:
+
+* read the backend base URL from `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`
+* call:
+  `POST ${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL}/api/v1/auth/login`
+* send credentials as:
+  `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`
+* map the email argument to the backend OAuth field:
+  `username`
+* send:
+  `password`
+* use `URLSearchParams` or an equivalent simple browser-supported approach
+* return the parsed JSON response on success
+* preserve the backend response fields:
+
+  * `access_token`
+  * `token_type`
+* throw a useful error if the request fails
+
+2. `getCurrentUser(token)`
+
+This function must:
+
+* call:
+  `GET ${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL}/api/v1/auth/me`
+* send:
+  `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
+* return the parsed user response on success
+* throw a useful error if the request fails
+
+Also:
+
+* throw a clear configuration error if `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` is missing
+* do not hardcode credentials
+* do not hardcode a JWT
+* do not use React hooks
+* do not add UI code
+* do not modify `dashboard-api.js`
+
+After making the change:
+
+1. List every file created or modified.
+2. Show both functions.
+3. Explain how form-urlencoded login works.
+4. Stop.
+

